    "license": "CC0-1.0 (intended)",
    "notes": "Wakaan Music Festival 2026 (6th edition), Oct 1-3 2026 at Mulberry Mountain Lodging & Events, 4117 Mulberry Mountain Loop, Ozark, AR 72949 (Franklin County, ~16 mi north of Ozark on AR-23 / Pig Trail). Early-arrival pass holders get 8am entry Wed Sep 30 plus a pre-party that night; GA gates open 1am Thu Oct 1; music runs early afternoon to just past sunrise nightly, ending around sunrise Sun Oct 4 (official event-info page). Pre-party (Sep 30) artists are not published, so no Sep 30 entries exist yet. LINEUP: all 62 billed acts (64 sets) transcribed from the official lineup poster (wakaanfestival.com, published 2026-08-19, explicitly 'in alphabetical order'); cross-checked against Festival Dust and JamBase (identical 62 names). Liquid Stranger and Truth are billed '(2 sets)' and appear twice. No per-day split has been published, so every entry has day = festival start date and note 'day unannounced'. STAGES: 2026 stage names have not been announced; ids reuse the 2025 layout (Aura main stage; Halo and Chakra late-night side stages, per The Daily Frequency's 2025 review). The official 2026 event-info page still refers to the 'Aura concert zone', so at least the main stage name appears to carry over. In 2025 the main stage ran early afternoon to ~2am and the side stages 2:30-6:30am. SET TIMES: none published as of 2026-09-11 (Festival Dust: 'before set times drop'); start/end are null on every entry. Expect an official set-times graphic on @wakaanfest (Instagram) / wakaanfestival.com in the final week before the festival (late September) - transcribe from that post, then fill day/night/stage. VENUE COORDS: 35.7118, -93.7972 is the venue's geocoded street address as listed on Songkick's venue page (35.71178, -93.79719); a second listing directory gives 35.7116, -93.7964 (~100 m apart). Not a surveyed stage position, so approximate: true. No OSM data used. MAP: stubs only; medical/entrance/water labels come from the official festival-faqs and event-info pages (no map published yet)."
